+### Requirement: POC-REQ-014 — Every work item's governing intent is a recorded edge or a counted Unknown
+
+Group: Work-item observation. Form: **invariant**.
+
+**Required behavior.** Every served work item SHALL carry a governing-intent
+field (`governedBy`). The field SHALL hold either an edge to the warrant the
+item was materialized under, joined by a recorded identity, or `Unknown` with
+exactly one primary reason from RFC2-24's closed list and that reason's
+resolution route. The POC SHALL NOT derive an edge from a work item's title,
+or from any other work-item text, by matching, similarity or inference. Both
+channels SHALL serve, over the served item set, how many items carry an edge
+and how many are Unknown. Trajectory SHALL mark each Unknown item, show the
+count, and let a reader narrow the board to the Unknown items. An Unknown item
+SHALL NOT be rendered as warranted, green or complete, and SHALL NOT be
+labelled orphaned work.
+
+- **Scope.** every served work item in the machine answer and on Trajectory.
+  This requirement admits no work-item column and no other input: the
+  projection stays as POC-REQ-010 to POC-REQ-013 bound it. While no admitted
+  input carries a warrant, every served item is Unknown with the reason
+  `source-uncaptured-or-unreachable`.
+
+- **Case (sweep + counterexample schema)**: a checker enumerates every served
+  work item from the machine answer — the denominator is the complete served
+  item set (POC-REQ-011) — and reads each item's `governedBy`. Separately, the
+  checker plants one fixture item whose title names a requirement identifier,
+  for example "Implement POC-REQ-010", and observes it.
+- **Observable**: each item's `governedBy` value; the served edge and Unknown
+  counts on both channels; Trajectory's Unknown markers, its count and its
+  narrowed view.
+- **Oracle**: every enumerated item carries exactly one of an edge with its
+  recorded join identity or an Unknown with one reason from RFC2-24's twelve;
+  the edge count plus the Unknown count equals the enumerated item count; the
+  two channels serve the same two counts; Trajectory's narrowed view lists
+  exactly the items the machine answer serves as Unknown; and the planted
+  item's `governedBy` is Unknown, never an edge to the identifier its title
+  names. Equality and set membership decide.
+- **Oracle independence**: the denominator is the checker's own enumeration
+  of served items, not the served counts; the reason list is read from
+  RFC2-24; the planted title is the checker's own.
+- **Falsifier**: a served item with no `governedBy`; an edge with no recorded
+  join identity; an edge whose only basis is work-item text; counts that do
+  not reconcile with the enumeration or differ between the channels; an
+  Unknown with no reason, a reason outside the twelve, or no route; or an
+  Unknown item rendered as warranted, green, complete or orphaned.
+
+#### Scenario: No admitted input carries a warrant
+
+- **WHEN** the machine answer serves N work items and no admitted input
+  carries a warrant
+- **THEN** both channels serve 0 items with an edge and N Unknown with the
+  reason `source-uncaptured-or-unreachable` and its route, and Trajectory
+  marks all N and lets a reader narrow the board to them
+
+#### Scenario: A title names a requirement
+
+- **WHEN** a served item's title reads "Implement POC-REQ-010"
+- **THEN** that item's `governedBy` is Unknown, and no edge to
+  POC-REQ-010 is served for it
+
+```yaml
+warrants:
+  primary: VIS-2
+  doctrine: [VIS-1, VIS-2, VIS-6]
+  contracts: [RFC2-24, RFC4-15, RFC8-22, RFC8-23]
+  policies: []
+  decisions: []
+  topology: []
+  parent_requirements: []
+```
+
